Qt 6.11.1 (qtbase) — fix the QMainWindow dock layout FREEZING after a dock is
torn out and left floating (all platforms).

This is a local backport of the UPSTREAM fix on the qt/qtbase 6.11 branch
(heading to 6.11.2; also on 6.12/dev) — commit e9a22af5ab7f "QDockWidget:
Clear saved state in begin / end drag", Fixes: QTBUG-147209. We independently
root-caused + fixed it the same way, then aligned to Qt's exact form (both
call sites). DROP this local patch once building against Qt >= 6.11.2.

SYMPTOM (QTBUG-147209 "Undocked QDockWidget prevents QMainWindow contents
from responding to resize"): drag a dock out of the main window and leave it
floating. From that moment the dock layout stops responding: the remaining
dock(s) do not grow into the freed space, and RESIZING THE MAIN WINDOW no
longer resizes the dock area — a dead zone appears at the window edge, dock
title-bar buttons fall outside the visible area when the window shrinks.
Everything snaps back the moment any dock is dropped INTO the layout again.

WHY: QMainWindowLayout::setGeometry() refuses to (re)fit the layout while a
drag snapshot exists ("if (savedState.isValid() || ...) return;"). The
snapshot is taken in QMainWindowLayout::unplug() at drag start. The
drop-into-layout path clears it (animationFinished -> savedState.clear());
the stay-floating path ran restore(QInternal::KeepSavedState) — never
clearing it, freezing every subsequent setGeometry().

This is a 6.11.1-ONLY regression: commit 650e2ed26920 (6.11 cherry-pick of
dev 1047809eb9bd, "Code cleanup in QMainWindowLayout" — a bool->enum
"bool trap" refactor, landed after v6.11.0) converted the old
restore(bool keepSavedState = false) DEFAULT-CLEAR call sites to the INVERTED
restore(QInternal::KeepSavedState). Qt <= 6.11.0 cleared here for years.
KeepSavedState remains correct for the restore() calls made WHILE a drag is
in progress (hover leaving a drop zone keeps the reference snapshot); the
startDrag ctrl-drag and endDrag stay-floating sites are terminal for the
snapshot and must clear.

JV-confirmed on Windows 11 / Qt 6.11.1 / MSVC x64: after tear-off the
remaining dock refits and main-window resizes track again; drop-into-layout,
splits and group dragging unaffected.

Apply to every platform's patched Qt tree (Windows
Projects\qt-static\qtbase-everywhere-src-6.11.1, macOS/Linux
~/Qt-6.11.1-patched) and rebuild QtWidgets. Re-apply after any qtbase source
refresh (< 6.11.2), then rebuild+install. Companion of
qtbase-6.11.1-dockgroup-dissolution.patch (same 6.11 dock-rework family).

--- a/src/widgets/widgets/qdockwidget.cpp
+++ b/src/widgets/widgets/qdockwidget.cpp
@@ void QDockWidgetPrivate::startDrag(DragScope scope)
     if (state->ctrlDrag)
-        layout->restore(QInternal::KeepSavedState);
+        layout->restore(QInternal::ClearSavedState);

     state->dragging = true;
@@ void QDockWidgetPrivate::endDrag(EndDragMode mode)
         if (mode == EndDragMode::Abort || !mwLayout->plug(state->widgetItem)) {
             if (hasFeature(this, QDockWidget::DockWidgetFloatable)) {
                 // This QDockWidget will now stay in the floating state.
                 if (state->ownWidgetItem) {
                     delete state->widgetItem;
                     state->widgetItem = nullptr;
                 }
-                mwLayout->restore(QInternal::KeepSavedState);
+                mwLayout->restore(QInternal::ClearSavedState);
                 QDockWidgetLayout *dwLayout = qobject_cast<QDockWidgetLayout*>(layout);
